% Bibliography for "Tu RNN den Transformer".
%
% Grouped by the chapter that first cites an entry, under %--- banners, per the
% house style. Only the six core papers are here: every one of them was read off
% the PDF in the author's papers folder, and each entry records the exact arXiv
% version that copy is, because page-anchored quotations in the chapters will
% refer to that copy rather than to a proceedings reprint with different
% pagination.
%
% Bridge papers (Ba 2016, Xiong 2020, BERT, GPT, Kaplan, Hoffmann,
% FlashAttention, RoPE, ALiBi, S4, Mamba, Swin, DeiT, ConvNeXt and the rest
% named in the SPEC's table of contents) are deliberately absent until needed.
% Each lands in the chapter that cites it, after that chapter's research step
% has fetched and read it: an entry added from memory is exactly the failure the
% research gate exists to prevent. The ones already here arrived that way - Cho
% 2014a and 2014b, Gers 2000 and 2002, Graves 2013 and Kalchbrenner 2013 in the
% chapter 04 and 05 sessions, Luong 2015, Schuster 1997 and Pouget-Abadie 2014
% in the chapter 06 one.
%
% An entry's `note` says how much of that paper was actually read. Three were
% cited from less than a full read and each said so; chapter 06 closed one of
% them, and Kalchbrenner 2013, Schuster 1997 and Pouget-Abadie 2014 remain
% record-only citations used for attribution and nothing else.

